      "message": "feat(vise): self-centering grip jaw - a step the stock sits on\n\nThe self-centering vise gains an optional grip step beside the dovetail\nlip: grip_depth (ledge below the jaw top) and grip_width (ledge reach\nfrom the clamping face), 0 = off. The jaw mesh carries the step and the\nframe's z = 0 is the ledge, so the stock seats on it and the fixture\nlaws judge the stepped jaw. Refused by name: one figure without the\nother, both with a dovetail, depth >= jaw height, width >= jaw\nthickness, ledges meeting at the opening. Project key additive (written\nonly when on), dialog rows with tooltips, MCP dimensions.\n\nFixes #1274\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
